  <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>At DailyInsightDesk.com, operated by Etern Digital, we use cookies and similar technologies to understand site traffic and to operate affiliate links. This policy explains what they are and how you can control them.</p>
  <h2>2. What Are Cookies?</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. Sites use them to function, to remember preferences, and to understand visits.</p>
  <h2>3. Types of Cookies We Use</h2>
  <p>We may use session cookies, which expire when you close the browser, and persistent cookies, which remain for a set period.</p>
  <h2>4. Categories</h2>
  <h3>Essential cookies</h3>
  <p>These are required for basic operation, such as security and page delivery. The site does not offer a separate account login.</p>
  <h3>Analytics cookies</h3>
  <p>We use Google Analytics to understand which guides are read. Analytics cookies collect information about how visitors use the site. You can opt out with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.</p>
  <h3>Advertising cookies</h3>
  <p>If a third-party ad network is added later, it may set cookies to measure or personalize ads. You can review Google’s ad controls at <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.</p>
  <h3>Affiliate cookies</h3>
  <p>When you click an affiliate link, the merchant or network may set a cookie so a later purchase can be credited to this site. That is how the commission, if any, is attributed. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
  <h2>5. Third-Party Cookies</h2>
  <p>Analytics and affiliate partners set their own cookies under their own policies. We do not control those policies. Read them if you want the details.</p>
  <h2>6. Managing Cookies</h2>
  <p>You can refuse or delete cookies in your browser. Blocking them may affect measurement and affiliate attribution. It should not stop you from reading the guides. Chrome, Firefox, Safari, and Edge each document the steps in their help pages.</p>
  <h2>7. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy when our practices change. The new text will appear on this page.</p>
